[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65576,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myeloid sarcoma is a tumour mass composed of blasts and often partially maturing elements of myeloid lineage that effaces the architecture of an extramedullary site.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65577,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9930/3 Myeloid sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65578,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2A60.39 &amp; XH3L40 Myeloid sarcoma &amp; Myeloid sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65579,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> granulocytic sarcoma; monocytic sarcoma; extramedullary myeloid cell tumour; chloroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65580,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65581,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Any site in the female genital tract can be involved; ovary and uterus are most common {9331287; 16707383}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65582,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients may present with vaginal bleeding, dysmenorrhoea, or a mass. Some patients have a history or simultaneous evidence of acute myeloid leukaemia (AML) in blood and/or bone marrow.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65583,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The epidemiological features reflect those of AML or the blast phase of other myeloid neoplasms {26185307}. About 10% of patients with AML develop myeloid sarcoma {23280377}. There is a wide age range, with the median patient age being in the third or fourth decade of life.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65584,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is similar to that of AML.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65585,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytogenetic/molecular abnormalities are shared with AML {28574302}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65586,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Involved organs are often enlarged, have a fish-flesh cut surface, and are green when the neoplastic cells express myeloperoxidase.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65587,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These neoplasms diffusely replace tissues. A single-file pattern is common and mitoses are numerous. The cells have thin nuclear membranes, fine (blastic) chromatin, and pinpoint nucleoli. There can be admixed granulocytic precursors (e.g. eosinophilic myelocytes). Tumour cells are positive for granulocytic/monocytic-associated antigens: CD13, CD33, CD34 (blasts), CD43, CD68, KIT (CD117), myeloperoxidase, and lysozyme {9331287; 16707383; 26185307}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65588,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Wright&ndash;Giemsa or Diff-Quik smears highlight cytoplasmic granules.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65589,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Molecular analysis should be performed as needed.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65590,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> effacement of tissue architecture by an infiltrate of medium-sized blast cells; immunoreactivity for one or more granulocytic/monocytic markers.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> cytogenetic and molecular analysis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65591,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Evaluation for AML is required.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65592,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 494,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients require AML-type therapy {26185307}. Patients presenting with myeloid sarcoma have better outcomes than those with AML {18623376}. Complete remission and long-term survival have been achieved in some patients with myeloid sarcoma of the gynaecological tract {9331287; 16707383}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]